        "status": "ready",
        "duration_sec": 11.99,
        "words": []
      },
      "motion": "none",
      "overlay_text": "",
      "narration": "The video was eventually examined by two retired FBI forensic image analysts. They found no obvious evidence of fabrication or digital manipulation. However, they couldn't determine exactly what the footage showed."
    },
    {
      "shot_id": "s02_12",
      "scene": 2,
      "scene_title": "Champ",
      "start_sec": 145.736,
      "end_sec": 160.995,
      "duration_sec": 15.259,
      "image": {
        "path": "images/s02_12.png",
        "status": "ready"
      },
      "clip": null,
      "audio": {
        "path": "voiceover/s02_12.mp3",
        "status": "ready",
        "duration_sec": 14.759,
        "words": []
      },
      "motion": "none",
      "overlay_text": "",
      "narration": "There was another strange discovery. In 2003, researchers had recorded unusual sequences of underwater clicking sounds inside the lake. These sounds were interpreted as possible biological sonar, resembling the echolocation used by certain marine animals."
    },
    {
      "shot_id": "s02_13",
      "scene": 2,
      "scene_title": "Champ",
      "start_sec": 160.995,
      "end_sec": 173.485,
      "duration_sec": 12.49,
      "image": {
        "path": "images/s02_13.png",
        "status": "ready"
      },
      "clip": null,
      "audio": {
        "path": "voiceover/s02_13.mp3",
        "status": "ready",
        "duration_sec": 11.99,
        "words": []
      },
      "motion": "none",
      "overlay_text": "",
      "narration": "At the time, no known native animal in Lake Champlain had been documented using this kind of echolocation. The lake contains approximately 6.8 trillion gallons of water and more than 70 islands."
    },
    {
      "shot_id": "s02_14",
      "scene": 2,
      "scene_title": "Champ",
      "start_sec": 173.485,
      "end_sec": 189.685,
      "duration_sec": 16.2,
      "image": {
        "path": "images/s02_14.png",
        "status": "ready"
      },
      "clip": null,
      "audio": {
        "path": "voiceover/s02_14.mp3",
        "status": "ready",
        "duration_sec": 15.7,
        "words": []
      },
      "motion": "none",
      "overlay_text": "",
      "narration": "Champ has never been officially identified by scientists. But between the photographs, recordings, underwater sounds, and generations of eyewitness reports, the mystery refuses to disappear. And somewhere beneath those 400 feet of dark water, the legend of Champ continues."
    },
    {
      "shot_id": "s03_01",
      "scene": 3,
      "scene_title": "The Julia Beast",
      "start_sec": 189.685,
