        "status": "ready",
        "duration_sec": 9.796,
        "words": []
      },
      "motion": "none",
      "overlay_text": "MARCH 1, 1999",
      "narration": "On March 1, 1999, underwater listening equipment in the Southern Ocean detected a powerful low-frequency sound. The signal was eventually named Julia."
    },
    {
      "shot_id": "s03_05",
      "scene": 3,
      "scene_title": "The Julia Beast",
      "start_sec": 229.85,
      "end_sec": 236.306,
      "duration_sec": 6.456,
      "image": {
        "path": "images/s03_05.png",
        "status": "ready"
      },
      "clip": null,
      "audio": {
        "path": "voiceover/s03_05.mp3",
        "status": "ready",
        "duration_sec": 5.956,
        "words": []
      },
      "motion": "none",
      "overlay_text": "",
      "narration": "Its source was traced to an area of the Antarctic Ocean between the Bransfield Strait and Cape Adare."
    },
    {
      "shot_id": "s03_06",
      "scene": 3,
      "scene_title": "The Julia Beast",
      "start_sec": 236.306,
      "end_sec": 247.96,
      "duration_sec": 11.654,
      "image": {
        "path": "images/s03_06.png",
        "status": "ready"
      },
      "clip": null,
      "audio": {
        "path": "voiceover/s03_06.mp3",
        "status": "ready",
        "duration_sec": 11.154,
        "words": []
      },
      "motion": "none",
      "overlay_text": "16X SPEED",
      "narration": "The sound was so unusually low that the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration released an accelerated version, playing it at 16 times its original speed. And that's where the mystery begins."
    },
    {
      "shot_id": "s03_07",
      "scene": 3,
      "scene_title": "The Julia Beast",
      "start_sec": 247.96,
      "end_sec": 263.48,
      "duration_sec": 15.52,
      "image": {
        "path": "images/s03_07.png",
        "status": "ready"
      },
      "clip": null,
      "audio": {
        "path": "voiceover/s03_07.mp3",
        "status": "ready",
        "duration_sec": 15.02,
        "words": []
      },
      "motion": "none",
      "overlay_text": "2,624 FT",
      "narration": "Over time, the Julia recording inspired stories about an unbelievably enormous sea creature, with some fictional descriptions claiming it could reach 2,624 feet in length. That's nearly 27 times the length of a blue whale measuring 98 feet."
    },
    {
      "shot_id": "s03_08",
      "scene": 3,
      "scene_title": "The Julia Beast",
      "start_sec": 263.48,
      "end_sec": 271.373,
      "duration_sec": 7.893,
      "image": {
        "path": "images/s03_08.png",
        "status": "ready"
      },
      "clip": null,
      "audio": {
        "path": "voiceover/s03_08.mp3",
        "status": "ready",
        "duration_sec": 7.393,
        "words": []
      },
      "motion": "none",
      "overlay_text": "",
      "narration": "If such a creature stood vertically, it would extend more than one and a half times the total height of the Empire State Building, including its antenna."
    },
    {
      "shot_id": "s03_09",
      "scene": 3,
      "scene_title": "The Julia Beast",
      "start_sec": 271.373,
      "end_sec": 286.632,
      "duration_sec": 15.259,
      "image": {
        "path": "images/s03_09.png",
        "status": "ready"
      },
      "clip": null,
      "audio": {
        "path": "voiceover/s03_09.mp3",
        "status": "ready",
        "duration_sec": 14.759,
        "words": []
      },
      "motion": "none",
      "overlay_text": "",
      "narration": "According to these stories, Julia has massive fins capable of rotating 180 degrees, allowing its enormous body to change direction underwater. Some fictional versions even describe Julia as a rival of another famous sea monster known as Blue."
    },
    {
      "shot_id": "s03_10",
      "scene": 3,
      "scene_title": "The Julia Beast",
      "start_sec": 286.632,
      "end_sec": 299.096,
      "duration_sec": 12.464,
      "image": {
        "path": "images/s03_10.png",
        "status": "ready"
      },
      "clip": null,
      "audio": {
        "path": "voiceover/s03_10.mp3",
        "status": "ready",
        "duration_sec": 11.964,
        "words": []
      },
      "motion": "none",
      "overlay_text": "",
      "narration": "Because of its supposed size, Julia is often portrayed as one of the most powerful creatures in the ocean. Its enormous body is even imagined to contain enough meat to feed an entire country for years."
    },
    {
      "shot_id": "s03_11",
      "scene": 3,
      "scene_title": "The Julia Beast",
      "start_sec": 299.096,
      "end_sec": 316.001,
      "duration_sec": 16.905,
      "image": {
        "path": "images/s03_11.png",
        "status": "ready"
      },
      "clip": null,
      "audio": {
        "path": "voiceover/s03_11.mp3",
        "status": "ready",
        "duration_sec": 16.405,
        "words": []
      },
      "motion": "none",
      "overlay_text": "",
      "narration": "But here's the actual explanation. Scientists later connected the original Julia sound to a massive piece of Antarctic ice, most likely an iceberg that had become grounded. As the ice moved and interacted with the surrounding environment, it produced unusual sounds that traveled through the ocean."
    },
    {
      "shot_id": "s03_12",
      "scene": 3,
      "scene_title": "The Julia Beast",
      "start_sec": 316.001,
      "end_sec": 332.749,
      "duration_sec": 16.748,
      "image": {
        "path": "images/s03_12.png",
        "status": "ready"
      },
      "clip": null,
      "audio": {
        "path": "voiceover/s03_12.mp3",
        "status": "ready",
        "duration_sec": 16.248,
        "words": []
      },
      "motion": "none",
      "overlay_text": "",
      "narration": "So, there is no scientific evidence that a giant animal was responsible for the recording. Still, the name Julia survived. And what started as a strange underwater sound eventually inspired the legend of a creature supposedly larger than anything else living beneath the ocean."
    },
    {
      "shot_id": "s04_01",
